ants remain unchanged | Model-neutral; potentially fine |\n| `below`, `merge`, or `lane-*` owns the target/base commit | No |\n| `main` becomes reachable through an arbitrary metadata branch | No |\n| Equivalent HEAD and explicit-tip traversals produce different graphs | No |\n| Legacy TOML keeps duplicate `confidence` ownership | Separate normalization regression, not desired workspace behavior |\n\nConcrete examples:\n\n- `dependent_branch_on_base`: `3183e43` should remain shared target context owned by `main`; all `below-*` branches are empty identities.\n- `single_merge_into_main_base_ignores_archived_metadata`: `0cc5a6f` remains target/main context; `merge` should not own it.\n- `tips_equivalent_to_workspace_metadata_are_order_independent`: an extra anonymous segment for only the explicit-tip traversal is unambiguously wrong.\n- `dlib_rs_auto_fix`: retaining duplicate `confidence` in the outside stack does not follow from `parent ^target`; it just weakens legacy cleanup.\n\nThe temporary commit’s target-bounded `Workspace` snapshots are aligned with the intended model. The extra 36 failures from removing reconciliation compatibility are not required to achieve that model—`into_workspace()` is already target-bounded. They are fallout from changing `workspace_upgrades()`’s mutation scope.\n\nThe acceptance rule should be:\n\n> Active commits equal each workspace parent minus `target_commit_id` and its ancestors; target history may remain only as base/status context; graph ownership must not depend on metadata or traversal spelling.\n\nOne unrelated repo-state note: [init.rs]([REDACTED:path]) currently has a stray `I w` before `pub fn`, so the worktree will not compile until that is removed. I left it untouched.\n\n<oai-mem-citation>\n<citation_entries>\nMEMORY.md:38-43|note=[used authoritative target commit membership and projection boundary guidance]\n<[REDACTED:path]>\n<rollout_ids>\n[REDACTED:entropy]\n[REDACTED:entropy]\n<[REDACTED:path]>\n<[REDACTED:path]>",